1. Transformation filters: Check filter() or where() conditions in PySpark to identify whether 500 rows were removed due to business rules or incorrect filter conditions.

2. Duplicate handling: Check whether dropDuplicates() or distinct() removed duplicate records from the source data.

3. Null keys: Check whether key columns contain NULL values and whether records were excluded using filter(), dropna(), or join conditions.
6. Incremental logic: Check watermark values, timestamps, and CDC conditions to ensure no records were skipped because of incorrect last-processed timestamps or incremental filters

